==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Easy to aim with.
* Great mobility.
* Both moves drain a lot of [[Instinct]] dodges if used in rapid succession (up to 7 dodges in a second).

|'''[Z] Piercing Dash'''
* No end-lag (you can literally use any move during Z's rushing animation).
* Drains a decent amount of [[Instinct]] dodges.

|'''[X] Scattering Gust'''
* The dark pink effect can annoy enemies.
* The slashes have long range.
* Decent hitbox.
* Allows the user to attack a chasing enemy while simultaneously getting further from them.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Hard to grind with due to the dashes during the M1 attacks, which occur on the first and the third click.

|'''[Z] Piercing Dash'''
* Rushing effect can be hard to combo with.
* Small hitbox.
* Short range compared to other swords' mobility moves.

|'''[X] Scattering Gust'''
* Difficult to land all the projectiles.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Canvander is used by the "Besto Friendo" [[NPC]] summoned by [[Love]]'s {{Ability|Love|V}}.
* The [[Musketeer Pirate]]s use Canvander, but don't have access to using the special abilities, therefore being restricted to the M1's instead.
* There is a glitch that when Canvander's {{Ability|TAP}} do not load in and the player uses an auto-clicker set to 1 millisecond intervals between each click, the player will fly in the air (this also works with other swords with dashes on [M1] attacks, such as [[Koko]].
** It also works if the player clicks on and off the sword while tapping the M1.
* There is a glitch that will make the petals in {{Ability|X}} go in different directions if the player turns their camera (or moves their cursor) fast enough.
* {{Ability|X}} can perform a similar movement trick to [[Skull Guitar]] M1 glitch where it launches the player forward a great distance if performed correctly. But unlike the bug, Canvander does not rely on players speed.
* Canvander has similar moves to the [[Cutlass]]/[[Katana]].
* The lunge M1s can glitch the player through thin walls, like the breakable wall at [[Kingdom of Rose]] that is located on the smaller wall close to [[Pirate Recruiter]]. 

